────────────────────────────────────────
AUTHORIZATION: RBAC + REQUEST ACCESS (C1)
────────────────────────────────────────

This system has TWO layers of authorization:
A) Tenant RBAC permissions (capabilities)
B) Request-level access rules (C1) (visibility / sharing / participants)

Never confuse them. Both must be enforced server-side.

────────────────────────────────────────
A) TENANT RBAC (Permissions)
────────────────────────────────────────

Roles (system roles in v1):
- OWNER
- ADMIN
- FINANCE
- MEMBER

Permission catalog (v1) includes (examples):
Tenant admin:
- tenant.audit.read
- tenant.billing.manage
- tenant.settings.manage
- tenant.roles.read
- tenant.roles.manage
- tenant.users.read
- tenant.users.invite
- tenant.users.manage
Requests:
- tenant.requests.create
- tenant.requests.read_all
- tenant.requests.close
- tenant.requests.share
- tenant.requests.link
- tenant.requests.export
Evidence:
- tenant.evidence.add
Approvals:
- tenant.approvals.assign_internal
- tenant.approvals.assign_external
- tenant.approvals.remind
Payments:
- tenant.payments.manage

RBAC rules:
1) Owner/Admin/Finance should generally have supersets of permissions.
2) RBAC checks must be done in the API handler (not middleware allowlists).

────────────────────────────────────────
B) REQUEST ACCESS RULES (C1)
────────────────────────────────────────

Rule of visibility for a request/record:
A user can access a request if ANY is true:
- user is creator
- user is an internal participant/approver on that request
- user has RequestAccess (viewer) created via sharing
- user has tenant.requests.read_all (Finance/Admin/Owner)

All list endpoints MUST filter by access rules, unless read_all.

Implement a shared helper:
- canAccessRequest({ tenantId, userId, requestId }): boolean

────────────────────────────────────────
CREATOR-ONLY APPROVALS MANAGEMENT (v1 decision)
────────────────────────────────────────

In v1:
- Members may assign approvers and send reminders ONLY for requests they created.
- Members do NOT have tenant-wide approvals permissions.

Therefore:
- canAssignInternalApprover(request, user) is true if:
  - isCreator(request, user) OR hasPermission("tenant.approvals.assign_internal")
- canAssignExternalApprover(request, user) is true if:
  - isCreator(request, user) OR hasPermission("tenant.approvals.assign_external")
- canSendReminder(request, user) is true if:
  - isCreator(request, user) OR hasPermission("tenant.approvals.remind")

Approval ACTION (approve/reject) is NOT governed by tenant.approvals.* permissions:
- Internal: only if user is the assigned pending approver
- External: only if token is valid and not expired/revoked

────────────────────────────────────────
CONSISTENCY REQUIREMENTS
────────────────────────────────────────

- Never leak whether a request exists to unauthorized users:
  - Prefer 404 for "not found" when access is missing (optional policy),
  - or 403 consistently if you prefer explicit forbidden.
- Do not return data across tenants under any circumstances.
- Every endpoint must decide access using the shared helpers.
